on" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-339138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f11112cb65b3e750933ec31424c8747ef9562283a56dd3eadf84f0b9e159d1c"} {"question" "q-339138" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-339138" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] ["math" "{e}^{-3x}"] ["math" "{e}^{3x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-339138" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{-3x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-339138" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-339138" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C{e}^{-3x}"] ["math" "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{-3x}"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-339138" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{2}+C{e}^{3x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-339140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{5}{x}y=7,\\,x>0.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below:\n\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The general solution is given by $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-339140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{5}{x}$ and $Q(x)=7.$ We proceed to find an integrating factor $I(x)$ using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (5/x)\\,dx} \\\\  & ={e}^{5\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{5})} \\\\  & ={x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply our differential equation through by $I(x)={x}^{5}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{5}{x}y) & ={x}^{5}\\cdot 7 \\\\ {x}^{5}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5{x}^{4}y & =7{x}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rewrite the left hand side as $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y\\cdot I(x))$ and carry out the integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{d}{dx}(y{x}^{5})\\,dx & =\\int 7{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{5} & =\\frac{7{x}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-339140" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f11112cb65b3e750933ec31424c8747ef9562283a56dd3eadf84f0b9e159d1c"} {"question" "q-339140" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-339140" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] ["math" "{x}^{4}"] ["math" "{x}^{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-339140" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-339140" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-339140" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}"] ["math" "\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}"] ["math" "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{4}}"] ["math" "x+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-339140" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{7x}{6}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{5}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x},\\,x>0,\\,y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}y) & =x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(yx)\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ yx & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+C}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{2C}{\\pi } \\\\ C & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2x}-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f11112cb65b3e750933ec31424c8747ef9562283a56dd3eadf84f0b9e159d1c"} {"question" "q-335812" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335812" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] ["math" "x"] ["math" "{e}^{x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335812" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335812" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335812" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\pi +3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi +4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335812" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi -2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2x}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=2x{e}^{-x},\\,y(0)=-2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=1$ and $Q(x)=2x{e}^{-x}.$ \n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y) & ={e}^{x}\\cdot 2x{e}^{-x} \\\\ {e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{x}y & =2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x}) & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{x} & ={x}^{2}+C \\\\ y & =({x}^{2}+C){e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =({0}^{2}+C){e}^{-0} \\\\ -2 & =(0+C)\\cdot 1 \\\\ C & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f11112cb65b3e750933ec31424c8747ef9562283a56dd3eadf84f0b9e159d1c"} {"question" "q-335806" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335806" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x"] ["math" "{e}^{-x}"] ["math" "{e}^{x}"] ["math" "{x}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335806" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335806" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335806" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(x-2){e}^{-x}"] ["math" "(x-2){e}^{x}"] ["math" "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}"] ["math" "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{x}"] ["math" "-2{e}^{-x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335806" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "({x}^{2}-2){e}^{-x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\nx\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=4{x}^{2},\\,y(1)=2\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The first step is to write the equation in standard form,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,.\n$$\n\nIn doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y & =4{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}(x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y) & =\\frac{1}{x}\\cdot 4{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y & =4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{2}{x},\\,Q(x)=4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot 4x \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =4{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & =4{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int 4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & ={x}^{4}+C \\\\ y & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(1)=2$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & ={1}^{2}+\\frac{C}{{1}^{2}} \\\\ 2 & =1+C \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f11112cb65b3e750933ec31424c8747ef9562283a56dd3eadf84f0b9e159d1c"} {"question" "q-335810" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335810" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x"] ["math" "{e}^{2x}"] ["math" "{e}^{x}"] ["math" "{x}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335810" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335810" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335810" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3x-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "3{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335810" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=8,\\,y(0)=-1\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=4$ and $Q(x)=8.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{4x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{4x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y) & ={e}^{4x}\\cdot 8 \\\\ {e}^{4x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4{e}^{4x}\\cdot y & =8{e}^{4x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{4x}) & =8{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{4x})\\text{d}x & =\\int 8{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{4x} & =8(\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x})+C \\\\ y{e}^{4x} & =2{e}^{4x}+C \\\\ y & =2+C{e}^{-4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=-1$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =2+C{e}^{-4(0)} \\\\ -1 & =2+C(1) \\\\ C & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=2-3{e}^{-4x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335829" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f11112cb65b3e750933ec31424c8747ef9562283a56dd3eadf84f0b9e159d1c"} {"question" "q-335829" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335829" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4x"] ["math" "{e}^{2x}"] ["math" "{e}^{4x}"] ["math" "{e}^{8x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335829" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{4x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335829" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335829" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "-{e}^{4x}"] ["math" "1-2{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "2-3{e}^{-4x}"] ["math" "4-5{e}^{4x}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335829" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2-3{e}^{-4x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335811" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2y}{x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}},\\,y(\\pi )=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335811" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{2}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}.$ \n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (2/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={x}^{2}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{2}{x}\\cdot y) & ={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{x}^{2})\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{x}^{2} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(\\pi )=0$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\pi ) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+C}{{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{C}{{\\pi }^{2}} \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14043121/state.json" "file_sha256" "262ce129f7f1f65c402783c2d66bedb70122542fa8239199acd5449d117bec1a"} {"question" "q-335811" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/